---
// About: the brand page, opened by the Good Call mark at the end of the tab bar.
// What Good Call is and stands for, how it works, its colours, the photo
// credits, and the disclaimer.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Wordmark from '../components/Wordmark.astro';
import { calls } from '../lib/site';
import { COINS } from '../lib/game';
import { photos } from '../lib/photos';

const palette = [
  { name: 'British Racing Green 4', hex: '#050602', role: 'The deepest shade, behind everything in dark mode. Steady and quiet.' },
  { name: 'British Racing Green', hex: '#004225', role: 'Our heritage green, for covers and the glow behind each page.' },
  { name: 'Alpine Green', hex: '#005C4C', role: 'Buttons, progress and the mark. Growth, and going the right way.' },
  { name: 'Calm blue', hex: '#2F6690', role: 'Streaks and information. Chosen to slow the pulse, not raise it.' },
  { name: 'Gold', hex: '#D9B44A', role: 'Coins and achievements. Warmth, and effort worth celebrating.' },
];
// Every photographer, once, however many photos of theirs are used.
const credits = [...new Map(Object.values(photos).map((photo) => [photo.by, photo])).values()];
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="What Good Call is and stands for, how it works, how answers are judged, its colours, photo credits and the disclaimer."
  path="/about/"
  tab="about"
>
  <section class="me" aria-labelledby="about-title">
    <span class="brand-hero" aria-hidden="true"><Wordmark /></span>
    <h1 id="about-title">About Good Call</h1>
    <p class="lead">Practise the call before it counts.</p>
  </section>

  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      Good Call is practice for judgement. Each scenario is a moment where the right thing to do is not obvious, or is
      obvious and still hard. You choose, and then you see the reasoning.
    </p>
    <p>
      It starts with consent, because that is where a bad call does the most harm, and because it is for everyone.
      Anyone can misjudge a situation. Anyone can have their own boundary ignored.
    </p>
    <p>
      The work scenarios are for people preparing for job applications and training, especially anyone who does not get
      the extra time or support to prepare. That includes many neurodivergent applicants. Timed tests reward people who
      already know the unwritten rules. Good Call writes the rules down.
    </p>
  </div>

  <section class="card" aria-labelledby="values-title">
    <h2 id="values-title">What we stand for</h2>
    <ul class="ticks">
      <li><span><b>Respect.</b> Every scenario starts from everyone's right to be treated with dignity.</span></li>
      <li><span><b>Honesty.</b> Real situations, plainly told, without shaming anyone for not knowing yet.</span></li>
      <li><span><b>Calm.</b> No timers, no leaderboards and no pressure. Learning sticks when you feel safe.</span></li>
      <li><span><b>Privacy.</b> No account and no tracking. What you learn here stays with you.</span></li>
      <li><span><b>Care.</b> Support is always one tap away, and every course points to charities doing the real work.</span></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card" id="how" aria-labelledby="how-title">
    <h2 id="how-title">How it works</h2>
    <ul class="ticks">
      <li>Every course is a book. Open one to see its topics, then start reading.</li>
      <li>No timer. Take as long as you need.</li>
      <li>Every answer comes with its reason, the good ones too.</li>
      <li>One go at each scenario. Once you lock in an answer, it stays.</li>
      <li>Your character plays the main part. Finish a course to unlock something new for them to wear.</li>
      <li>
        Earn coins as you go: {COINS.best} for a good call, {COINS.okay} for one that could be better, {COINS.risky} for
        trying and {COINS.courseComplete} for finishing a course. Pledge them to a charity linked to what you learned.
      </li>
      <li>No account. Your progress is saved in this browser.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card" aria-labelledby="coins-title">
    <h2 id="coins-title">About coins and pledges</h2>
    <p>
      Coins are points, not money. They cannot be bought, sold or cashed in, and Good Call does not donate on your
      behalf. Pledging them is a way to say which causes matter to you, and every charity is linked so you can
      support it directly if you want to. We have no partnership with these charities and they do not endorse Good
      Call.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card" aria-labelledby="judged-title">
    <h2 id="judged-title">How answers are judged</h2>
    <p>Real situations are rarely just right or wrong, so there are three verdicts:</p>
    <ul class="ticks">
      <li><span><b>{calls.best.label}.</b> The choice that respects everyone involved and solves the problem.</span></li>
      <li><span><b>{calls.okay.label}.</b> It avoids the worst outcome but leaves something undone.</span></li>
      <li><span><b>{calls.risky.label}.</b> It is likely to hurt someone, or you.</span></li>
    </ul>
    <p>Every answer has its reason. The reason is the point, not the score.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="card" aria-labelledby="colours-title">
    <h2 id="colours-title">Our colours</h2>
    <ul class="palette">
      {
        palette.map((colour) => (
          <li>
            <span class="palette-swatch" style={`background: ${colour.hex}`} aria-hidden="true" />
            <span>
              <b>{colour.name}</b> <small>{colour.hex}</small>
              <span class="fine">{colour.role}</span>
            </span>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card" aria-labelledby="limits-title">
    <h2 id="limits-title">What this is not</h2>
    <ul class="ticks">
      <li>Not legal advice. Where a law is mentioned, it is the law in England and Wales unless it says otherwise.</li>
      <li>Not a qualification. Finishing a course does not certify anything.</li>
      <li>Not a mark scheme. Employers score their own tests in their own way.</li>
      <li>
        Not yet reviewed. These scenarios are first versions. They have not been checked by a consent educator, a
        lawyer or a recruiter.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card" id="disclaimer" aria-labelledby="disclaimer-title">
    <h2 id="disclaimer-title">Disclaimer</h2>
    <p>
      Good Call is provided for general education only. The scenarios, answers and reasons are teaching material.
      They are not legal, medical, psychological, safeguarding or employment advice, and they are no substitute for
      advice from a qualified professional about your own situation.
    </p>
    <p>
      Using this site, or completing any part of it, does not show that a person understands or follows what it
      teaches. It is not evidence of good character, and it is not a defence. Nothing here may be relied on to
      excuse, justify or defend antisocial, abusive, discriminatory or unlawful behaviour, by the person who used the
      site or by anyone else.
    </p>
    <p>
      Your answers are not used to build a profile of you. They are saved only in your own browser. They are never
      sent to Good Call, its author, an employer or anyone else, so they cannot be used to assess you, rank you,
      target you or discriminate against you.
    </p>
    <p>
      Everyone remains fully responsible for their own choices and actions. Good Call and its author accept no
      responsibility for how this material is used, or for any decision made or action taken because of it.
    </p>
    <p>
      The scenarios are fictional. Any resemblance to real people or events is coincidental. If you are in danger, or
      someone else is, call 999.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card" aria-labelledby="privacy-title">
    <h2 id="privacy-title">Your answers</h2>
    <p>
      You get one go at each scenario. Once you lock in an answer it cannot be changed, so your result is your real
      first judgement. Your answers and reading settings are saved in this browser only. Nothing is sent anywhere,
      there is no account and no tracking. To remove your answers from one course, use "Clear my answers and start
      again" at the end of it. To remove everything, use "Delete all my Good Call data" on your profile.
    </p>
  </section>

  {
    credits.length > 0 && (
      <section class="card" aria-labelledby="credits-title">
        <h2 id="credits-title">Photo credits</h2>
        <p>
          Photos are from <a href="https://unsplash.com/">Unsplash</a>, used under the{' '}
          <a href="https://unsplash.com/license">Unsplash Licence</a>. Thank you to:
        </p>
        <ul class="credits">
          {credits.map((photo) => (
            <li>
              <a href={photo.page} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                {photo.by}
              </a>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
        <p class="fine">Book covers and characters are drawn for Good Call.</p>
      </section>
    )
  }
</Base>
